  "id": "chemical-transmission",
  "term": "chemical transmission",
  "definition": "Chemical transmission is the process at a synapse in which synaptic proteins work together to release neurotransmitter efficiently. In this context, successful signaling depends on coordinated protein function, including calcium-sensitive mechanisms involved in fast, synchronized release.",
